       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is a dose that causes acute liver injury, and I don't know of any clinical setting where it's appropriate. Normal liver function, weight and kidney function don't change that. Entering it would put the patient at serious risk.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard-range order right away.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day) or 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2,600 mg/day).\n- **Enter the order with a note** if a different intent is behind this. For example, if the order is meant to be 3,000 mg total per day, I can enter it with the right per-dose amount and frequency.\n- **Bring in pharmacy.** If you think there's a rationale I'm missing, such as a protocol or a unit conversion, a pharmacist can review it with you. They can also enter it through a pathway with appropriate safety checks.\n\nWhich of these would you like?"
      }
